Common SQL Data Types 
> Data types define what kind of data a column can store in a table

Data Type                         What It Stores                                   Typical Uses
INT                           Whole Whole numbers(no decimals)                   IDs (user_id, order_id), counts (quantity, attempt_count), ages
BIGINT                        Very large whole numbers                           Huge row counts, global counters, high-traffic logs
VARCHAR(n)                    Variable-length text up top characters             Names, emails, usernames, short labels
TEXT                          Long, unbounded text                               Product descriptions, blog posts, long reviews
Date                          Calendar date only (YYYY-MM-DD)                    Birthdate, signup date, holidays, due dates
DateTime/Timestamp            Date + time (optionally timezone/offset)           Order creation time, payment time, login timestamps, event logs
